      "math_academy_id": "e-3246",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\tan K.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224552/assets/fbac8700b860cbe8a60f2c24a5ab7ee9e7adfda584b1077edf208b0dcd16744e.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the definition of tangent: \n\n$$\n\\tan K = \\dfrac {\\textrm{opposite}}{\\textrm{adjacent}} = \\dfrac {JL}{JK} = \\dfrac{JL}{7.5}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing side $JL.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nJL &= \\sqrt{ KL^2 - JK^2 } \\\n&= \\sqrt{ 12.5^2 - 7.5^2 } \\\n&= \\sqrt{ 156.25-56.25 } \\\n&= \\sqrt{100 }\\\n&= 10\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\tan K&= \\dfrac{JL}{7.5}\\[5pt]\n &= \\dfrac{10}{7.5}  \\[5pt]\n &=\\dfrac 4 3.\n\t}\n$$",
